What is the botanical classification system used to categorize orchids?
The botanical classification system used to categorize orchids varies across different taxonomic systems. Some of the systems mentioned in the context include:

* Bentham & Hooker: Orchids in order "Microspermae"
* Engler system: Orchids in order "Microspermae"
* Wettstein system: Orchids in order "Gynandrae"
* Dahlgren system: Orchids in one family or divided into more families
* Takhtajan system: Orchids in order "Orchidales"
* Cronquist system (1981): Orchids in order "Orchidales"
* Thorne system (1992): Orchids in order "Orchidales"
* APG II system: Orchids in order "Asparagales"

Note that the classification of orchids can vary depending on the system used, and some systems may group them differently.
